BLOCKER-1 [OWNER: TEAM 1 + TEAM 2] — API/frontend integration
  Symptom: pages.dev/api/* does NOT reach the Worker. POST /api/auth/login -> 405;
  GET /api/kasir/reminder-closing -> 200 SPA index.html; /_redirects served as HTML.
  Root cause: Cloudflare Pages _redirects proxying ONLY supports relative URLs —
  external domains CANNOT be proxied (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/,
  "Proxying will only support relative URLs on your site. You cannot proxy external domains.")
  and 200-status proxy is GET-only. The chosen same-origin _redirects proxy to
  irkop-cell-backend.irkop.workers.dev is unsupported. Worker has no CORS headers, so
  direct cross-origin frontend->worker also fails in a browser.
  Verified recommended fix (a): frontend Pages Function functions/[[path]].js that
  forwards all methods to the Worker (no CORS needed, works on *.pages.dev).
  Alternative fix (b): add CORS middleware to Worker + set VITE_API_BASE to worker URL.

BLOCKER-2 [OWNER: TEAM 1] — No bootstrap admin user
  Symptom: production users table is empty; login cannot succeed.
  Root cause: no seed/CLI/documented procedure creates the first user; the only
  createUser route (backend/src/routes/users.js) requires an existing admin (chicken-egg).
  Required fix: documented first-admin bootstrap (e.g., one-time creation script or
  guarded first-run endpoint) OR operator-run SQL insert using the app's PBKDF2-SHA256
  210k-iteration hash (backend/src/lib/password.js). Live smoke/financial gates are blocked
  on this.

